      <h1 id="set-up-your-tools" class="group scroll-mt-20">Set up your tools<a href="#set-up-your-tools" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h1>
      <p>The tutorial needs two tools: DITA-OT, which publishes the guide, and the DogsBay XML command line <code>dogsbay-xml</code>, which validates the files and checks the project. The gate script finds both on your <code>PATH</code> or through two environment variables.</p>
      <p>You also need git and a text editor. The DogsBay XML editor is the recommended editor: it validates as you type against the same DTDs the gate uses, and it ships the command line. Any editor that can save UTF-8 text works.</p>
      <h2 id="install-dita-ot-435" class="group scroll-mt-20">Install DITA-OT 4.3.5<a href="#install-dita-ot-435" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <p>The gate and the tutorial are verified against DITA-OT 4.3.5. Other 4.x releases probably work; 4.3.5 is known to.</p>
      <Steps>
      <Step>
      <strong>Download the release</strong> Get <code>dita-ot-4.3.5.zip</code> from the <a href="https://github.com/dita-ot/dita-ot/releases/tag/4.3.5">DITA-OT releases</a> and unpack it somewhere you keep tools, such as <code>~/Downloads/dita-ot-4.3.5</code> or <code>/opt/dita-ot-4.3.5</code>.
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Check it runs</strong> DITA-OT needs a Java runtime, 17 or later.
      <CodeBlock code={"~/Downloads/dita-ot-4.3.5/bin/dita --version"} lang="bash" />
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Tell the gate where it is</strong> The gate looks for <code>dita</code> on your <code>PATH</code>, then at <code>DITA_HOME</code>, then at the default <code>~/Downloads/dita-ot-4.3.5</code>. If you unpacked it elsewhere, set the variable in your shell profile:
      <CodeBlock code={"export DITA_HOME=/opt/dita-ot-4.3.5"} lang="bash" />
      </Step>
      </Steps>
      <h2 id="install-the-dogsbay-xml-command-line" class="group scroll-mt-20">Install the DogsBay XML command line<a href="#install-the-dogsbay-xml-command-line" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <p><code>dogsbay-xml</code> is installed with the DogsBay XML editor. The installer puts the executable beside the editor, and the command line needs neither a running editor nor a separate JDK.</p>
      <Steps>
      <Step>
      <strong>Install the editor</strong> Follow <a href="https://dogsbay.ai/dogsbay-xml-docs/getting-started/install">Installing</a> in the DogsBay XML documentation: download the package for your platform from the <a href="https://github.com/dogsbay/dogsbay-xml/releases">releases page</a> and install it the usual way.
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Put the command line on your PATH</strong> The same page shows the directory for each platform. On Linux:
      <CodeBlock code={"export PATH=\"/opt/dogsbay-xml-editor/bin:$PATH\"\ndogsbay-xml --version"} lang="bash" />
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Or point the gate at it</strong> If you would rather not change your <code>PATH</code>, set <code>DOGSBAY_XML</code> to the executable. The gate checks the variable first, then the <code>PATH</code>.
      <CodeBlock code={"export DOGSBAY_XML=/opt/dogsbay-xml-editor/bin/dogsbay-xml"} lang="bash" />
      </Step>
      </Steps>
      <Alert variant="note" class="my-4">
        <AlertTitle>Note</AlertTitle>
        <AlertDescription>
          <p><code>xmllint</code> cannot stand in for <code>dogsbay-xml</code>. libxml2 refuses the DITA 1.3 DTDs with "Maximum entity amplification factor exceeded", even with <code>--huge</code>. <code>dogsbay-xml</code> validates with Xerces and the DITA-OT catalog.</p>
        </AlertDescription>
      </Alert>
      <h2 id="clone-the-repository" class="group scroll-mt-20">Clone the repository<a href="#clone-the-repository" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <Steps>
      <Step>
      <strong>Clone it</strong>
      <CodeBlock code={"git clone https://github.com/dogsbay/dogsbay-xml-dita-tutorial.git\ncd dogsbay-xml-dita-tutorial"} lang="bash" />
      <p>The clone opens on <code>main</code>, which is a different, finished project. Do not start from it.</p>
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Check out the first stage</strong>
      <CodeBlock code={"git checkout tutorial/00-setup"} lang="bash" />
      <p>The working tree is replaced: <code>tutorial/00-setup</code> shares no history with <code>main</code>. See <a href="/dogsbay-xml-dita-tutorial-docs/start-here/how-the-tutorial-works">How the tutorial works</a>.</p>
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Confirm where you are</strong>
